<title>USA: Venezuela's 1996 inflation seen at 95 pct - Matos.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's 1996 inflation seen at 95 pct - Matos.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan Finance Minister Luis Ral Matos Azcar said Friday the country's inflation for 1996 would come in at 95 percent, and December's inflation is expected to be about be two percent.</p>
<p>He told reporters the December figure would be above the government's target of 1.5 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we will be a little higher than that -- two percent,&quot; he said. &quot;On the whole, overall inflation for the year will be 95 percent.&quot;</p>
</text>
